# Changelog

## v0.4.0 (2026-05-21)

### Enhancements

- [Auth] Add Kerberos/Negotiate authentication via GSS.framework (macOS) — replaces Windows-only Negotiate in `proxyplease` with native macOS support using the system credential cache
- [Auth] No config changes required — `negotiateDial` hook is tried before `proxyplease`; uses `gss_acquire_cred(GSS_C_NO_CREDENTIAL)` so no password is needed when a valid TGT exists
- [Auth] Automatic fallback to NTLM/Basic via `proxyplease` if Negotiate fails (no TGT, wrong realm, proxy doesn't support it)
- [Auth] SPN constructed as `HTTP@<proxy-canonical-fqdn>` via forward+reverse DNS lookup — handles short names and CNAMEs commonly used in proxy URLs
- [Auth] Negotiate failure cache (30s TTL) — avoids hammering the KDC/proxy on repeated requests after a failure; cache cleared on config reload and on successful auth
- [Log] Change all package-level loggers from `LevelInfo` to `LevelDebug` so the `[log] level` config setting can control verbosity in both directions
- [Log] Add WARN-level message when both Negotiate and NTLM/Basic fail without any credentials configured

### Limitations

- [Auth] Second round (mutual auth) not yet handled — single-round Kerberos only
- [Auth] gokrb5 pure Go for Linux planned for v0.5.0
- [Auth] Auto-TGT acquisition from config password planned for v0.5.0

## v0.3.3 (2026-05-20)

### Bug fixes

- [MITM] Only trigger MITM when CONNECT host matches at least one route prefix — non-matching hosts use the normal tunnel, avoiding unnecessary TLS overhead and potential proxy blocks
- [MITM] Fix port missing from route target when dialing through upstream proxy — route URLs like `https://example.com` produce `Host: "example.com"` (no port), causing `CONNECT example.com:80` (default HTTP) instead of `CONNECT example.com:443`; the upstream proxy returned 403

## v0.3.2 (2026-05-19)

### Bug fixes

- [Routes] Revert "routed requests bypass upstream proxy" — routed requests again respect the location's upstream proxy; MITM bypass was causing routed requests to fail when the destination was only reachable through the corporate proxy

---

### Enhancements

- [Config] Add `routes` to `[defaults]` — routes defined here apply regardless of which location matches; location routes override same-key defaults
- [Log] Add structured logger with levels (`debug`, `info`, `warn`, `error`) and per-request correlation IDs — replaces raw `log.Printf`
- [Log] Add `[log]` section to config for setting log level (`level = "info"`)
- [Log] Add deduplicating logger for high-frequency messages (router decisions)
- [Log] Add `RedactURL` helper to prevent credential leakage in logs
- [Log] Promote MITM route-match messages to `info` level so routing decisions are visible

### Bug fixes

- [Reload] Add content-hash comparison to config reload — prevents spurious reloads on file "touch" without content changes
- [CLI] Replace `log.Fatalf` with clean error messages in `install`, `install-certs`, `migrate` commands
- [CI] Copy formula from source repo instead of sed-patching old tap formula — ensures tap always has the latest formula structure

## v0.3.0 (2026-05-13)

### Enhancements

- [Config] New configuration schema — `locations` replace `rules`, `proxies` map for named upstream definitions, `defaults` for fallback behavior
- [Config] Add `version` field to config for future schema migration support
- [Config] Named proxy definitions — define a proxy once, reference it by name from multiple locations
- [Config] Per-location `no_proxy` list — bypass proxy for specific destinations within a location; supports exact IP, CIDR, exact domain, `.domain` suffix match, and `*` wildcard
- [Config] `defaults.no_proxy` — additional always-direct destinations on top of the hardcoded `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, `::1`
- [Config] Location matchers — OR logic within each array (`ssids`, `ips`, `domains`), AND logic across arrays
- [Config] Validation on startup — unknown proxy names, locations without matchers, invalid URLs all abort with a clear error
- [Config] Legacy format detection — clear error message with link to documentation when old `upstream`/`rules` format is detected
- [Config] Auto-migrate new JSON config format to TOML (in addition to legacy format); `Load()` converts any JSON config seamlessly
- [Config] Stamped `version` during migration — migrated configs are version-tracked for future schema upgrades
- [Config] Add `routes` to `Location` — destination rewriting rules using URL prefix matching. Each route redirects matching `host+path` requests to a configurable base URL, like an API gateway.
- [Config] Add `Routes` field to `Decision` — carries the matched location's route map for per-request destination rewriting in the proxy handler
- [Router] `Decide()` no longer takes a `path` parameter — route resolution moved to the proxy handler

### Bug fixes

- [CI] Fix build on non-Darwin platforms by adding build tags to cgo files and no-op stubs for Linux and other platforms

### CLI

- [Migrate] Make `migrate` command idempotent for Homebrew `post_install` — exits cleanly when no legacy `config.json` exists or the JSON is not in legacy format, instead of fatally aborting
- [Certs] Add `install-certs` command — generates a local CA certificate for TLS MITM and prints platform-specific trust installation instructions
- [Help] Update help text to document TLS MITM, `install-certs`, and updated paths

### Proxy

- [MITM] Add TLS interception (MITM) for HTTPS CONNECT tunnels when a location has routes defined — enables path-based routing on HTTPS connections
- [MITM] Add `mitmProxy` method — forwards decrypted HTTP requests between client-side and target-side TLS connections within the MITM tunnel
- [MITM] Automatic CA certificate generation on first run; per-host certificates generated on-demand and cached in memory
- [Routes] `handleHTTP` applies route rewriting before forwarding — matched routes redirect the request to the route's target URL directly, bypassing the location proxy
- [Routes] `handleCONNECT` triggers MITM mode when the matched location has routes; each decrypted HTTP request is routed individually — unmatched requests go to the original host, matched requests are redirected to the route target
- [MITM] `mitmProxy` establishes a fresh TLS connection per request to the target determined by route matching; non-routed requests respect the location's upstream proxy, routed requests go direct

### Formula

- [Brew] Update service definition and `post_install` to use `config.toml`; run `migrate` and `install-certs` during install to auto-convert legacy configs and generate the CA

---

## v0.2.1 (2026-04-14)

### Bug fixes

- [Proxy] Fix add darwin build tags to cgo files, add stubs for other platforms

---

## v0.2.0 (2026-03-19)

### Enhancements

- [Proxy] Add `User-Agent` and `Proxy-Connection: Keep-Alive` headers to upstream CONNECT requests, matching real client behavior
- [Proxy] Add per-rule `dns` field — custom DNS servers used only for connections matching that rule, without touching system DNS settings
- [Proxy] Add automatic auth scheme negotiation via `proxyplease` — transparently handles Basic, NTLM, and Negotiate per-connection by inspecting `Proxy-Authenticate` on 407 responses
- [Config] Add `upstream_domain` field for Active Directory NTLM auth — keeps the upstream URL clean and parseable
- [Router] Log collapsed to single line per request — host shown only on rule match

### Bug fixes

- [Proxy] Fix recurring 407 Proxy Authentication Required after ~45 minutes — upstream switches from Basic to Negotiate on session expiry, now handled transparently
- [Proxy] Fix hang on CONNECT when upstream requires NTLM and domain is not provided
- [Proxy] Fix upstream URL parsing failure with `domain\user` or `domain/user` format in credentials
- [Proxy] Fix 407 authentication failures caused by missing `Proxy-Connection: Keep-Alive` header in CONNECT tunnel

---

## v0.1.5 (2026-03-19)

### Enhancements

- [Proxy] Add per-rule `dns` field — custom DNS servers used only for connections matching that rule, without touching system DNS settings
- [Proxy] Add comprehensive logging to all proxy error paths — 502 failures now include the exact reason
- [Config] Introduce `Decision` type returned by `Decide()`, carrying both action and DNS servers
- [Router] Add deduplicating logger — repeated identical entries are suppressed and summarized every 100 occurrences
- [Network] Add 250ms debounce and same-value guard to `networkDidChange` to coalesce rapid network events
- [Network] Move SSID cache seeding from `init()` to `StartNetworkListener()` — binary startup is now side-effect free for subcommands like `completion`, `version`, `help`
- [CLI] Add `unknown command` error for unrecognized subcommands instead of silently falling back to `run`
- [CLI] Redact upstream proxy password in logs using `url.Redacted()`

### Bug fixes

- [Proxy] Fix 502 errors caused by upstream proxy hostname DNS resolution failures on network switch
- [Network] Fix SSID change event firing twice per network transition due to duplicate `SCDynamicStore` key registration
- [Completion] Fix `completion bash` exiting with code 1 during Homebrew install due to `init()` side effects

---

